{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And if a man strikes any human soul.</b> Since among certain nations cursing Elohim is a very light matter, as it says: וְהִתְקַצַּף וְקִלֵּל בְּמַלְכּוֹ וּבֵאלֹהָיו (Isaiah 8:21), and as our Sages of blessed memory said (Sanhedrin 60a): \"One who hears the mention [of the Name] from the mouth of a gentile is not obligated to tear [his garments], for if you do not say so, the entire garment would be filled with tears.\" And moreover, it would appear that the speech of one who curses is null speech, since every curse is precluded by the existence of the blessed El. He explained the reason and said: for indeed an evil act, when performed upon different subjects, even though it is one act in itself, its punishment changes according to the change in those subjects, so that when the offence is upon a certain subject the punishment may be corporal or capital, and when it is upon a subject below that, the punishment is monetary. Concerning this he gave three proofs: first, regarding one who kills — one who kills a human soul is liable to death, while one who kills his fellow's animal is liable to monetary payment alone. Second, regarding one who injures — one who injures a person would deserve corporal punishment, were it not for our inability to administer it precisely, as our Rabbis of blessed memory received (Bava Kamma, chapter HaḤovel), so that monetary punishment was necessary. And even so, the monetary penalty is substantial, since he is liable for five things, as they of blessed memory received. And one who strikes an animal — his punishment is a small monetary penalty. Third, regarding one who injures a person — one who strikes his father or mother is liable to death, while one who strikes another person is liable monetarily, and needless to say one who strikes an animal in this manner, whose punishment is very slight. And he did not mention cursing one's father or mother, for it is not comparable to this curse [of Elohim], which is entirely null speech, whereas cursing a father is not so."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:37:49.488017516Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}